1
00:00:00,420 --> 00:00:03,007
Dependabot opened this pull request on my demo shop.

2
00:00:03,007 --> 00:00:05,740
It bumps React Query from version 4 to version 5.

3
00:00:05,740 --> 00:00:08,120
All three CI checks are green.

4
00:00:09,999 --> 00:00:11,459
This is the shop on that commit.

5
00:00:11,459 --> 00:00:12,419
The page is blank.

6
00:00:12,419 --> 00:00:16,339
The build passed, the tests passed, and the app does not render.

7
00:00:18,720 --> 00:00:20,400
CI checks that the code builds.

8
00:00:20,400 --> 00:00:21,840
It does not open the app.

9
00:00:21,840 --> 00:00:23,540
Bumpproof does.

10
00:00:24,869 --> 00:00:27,795
Bumpproof builds the base branch and the pull request in a

11
00:00:27,795 --> 00:00:28,949
Docker sandbox.

12
00:00:28,949 --> 00:00:32,682
Then Kane CLI drives a real Chrome through three journeys in

13
00:00:32,682 --> 00:00:36,409
plain English: browse, checkout, and the account page.

14
00:00:38,788 --> 00:00:40,895
On the base, all three journeys pass.

15
00:00:40,895 --> 00:00:42,788
On the pull request, all three fail.

16
00:00:42,788 --> 00:00:45,578
Kane says the Orders tab leads to a blank page.

17
00:00:45,578 --> 00:00:47,241
The browser console shows why:

18
00:00:47,241 --> 00:00:50,088
it cannot read "orders" of undefined.

19
00:00:52,472 --> 00:00:55,392
The verdict is written by code, not by a model.

20
00:00:55,392 --> 00:00:58,632
A journey that passes on the base and fails on the pull request

21
00:00:58,632 --> 00:01:00,252
is a regression.

22
00:01:02,630 --> 00:01:04,330
Then Claude Code gets the failure,

23
00:01:04,330 --> 00:01:06,363
the console error and the release notes.

24
00:01:06,363 --> 00:01:07,937
It has file tools only.

25
00:01:07,937 --> 00:01:09,217
No shell and no web.

26
00:01:09,217 --> 00:01:11,610
It may not change the bumped version.

27
00:01:13,989 --> 00:01:15,349
It changes two lines.

28
00:01:15,349 --> 00:01:18,576
In version 5 the "loading" status is called "pending".

29
00:01:18,576 --> 00:01:21,529
It quotes that line from the upgrade guide.

30
00:01:23,911 --> 00:01:27,258
The fix is built again, and Kane runs every journey again.

31
00:01:27,258 --> 00:01:28,727
Three of three pass.

32
00:01:28,727 --> 00:01:32,091
Only then does Bumpproof accept the fix.

33
00:01:34,461 --> 00:01:37,293
It posts one comment on the pull request: the table,

34
00:01:37,293 --> 00:01:39,074
what Kane saw, and the patch.

35
00:01:39,074 --> 00:01:41,288
It pushes the fix to the bot's branch.

36
00:01:41,288 --> 00:01:42,741
It does not merge.

37
00:01:42,741 --> 00:01:44,801
A person decides.

38
00:01:47,178 --> 00:01:51,658
That run took 22 minutes and 102 Kane credits.

39
00:01:51,658 --> 00:01:54,878
The fix cost 18 cents.

40
00:01:57,258 --> 00:02:00,838
On this repository it ran on three Dependabot pull requests.

41
00:02:00,838 --> 00:02:02,145
One was safe.

42
00:02:02,145 --> 00:02:03,438
React Query was fixed.

43
00:02:03,438 --> 00:02:05,938
The date-fns bump broke the build,

44
00:02:05,938 --> 00:02:08,958
and Claude Code fixed it in six lines.

45
00:02:11,333 --> 00:02:13,813
Then I ran it on other people's pull requests.

46
00:02:13,813 --> 00:02:15,733
14 repositories, read only.

47
00:02:15,733 --> 00:02:17,333
8 could run in the sandbox.

48
00:02:17,333 --> 00:02:18,293
7 were safe.

49
00:02:18,293 --> 00:02:21,273
1 broke the build, and the fixer did not fix it.

50
00:02:23,659 --> 00:02:27,259
To test for false alarms, I ran each base against itself.

51
00:02:27,259 --> 00:02:29,519
8 of 8 came back the same.

52
00:02:31,910 --> 00:02:35,574
In the census, no pull request had green CI and a broken app.

53
00:02:35,574 --> 00:02:38,170
This shop is the only case I have.

54
00:02:40,652 --> 00:02:42,412
Limits: npm only.

55
00:02:42,412 --> 00:02:45,012
Apps that need a database or secrets cannot run.

56
00:02:45,012 --> 00:02:49,232
A failing journey costs many times the credits of a passing one.

57
00:02:51,920 --> 00:02:55,140
Everything here comes from the run files in the repository.

58
00:02:55,140 --> 00:02:57,940
You can replay any run without a key.

